Controls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00064",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[53]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 8839,
      "endIndex": 8907,
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_1",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "5 Local adaptation through products, packaging and cultural contact",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00065",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[54]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 8907,
      "endIndex": 8956,
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_2",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "5.1 Imported materials and locally made products",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00066",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[55]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 8956,
      "endIndex": 9572,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Staff reported mainly Chinese imports for variety and cost, with limited local cultivation. Table A5 separates three meanings of “local”: grown, packaged or manufactured in Singapore. Cactus and roselle illustrate possible local cultivation, but shop-stock origins remain unconfirmed. Mind Soothe Capsules have a documented Singapore manufacturing link. Five Flower Tea and monk-fruit tea are external examples of local packaging and beverage production, not Tong Keow products. These distinctions illustrate adaptation through Singapore’s retail and production systems, even with imported ingredients (Yang, 2022).",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00067",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[56]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 9572,
      "endIndex": 10244,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "HSA lists Nature’s Green Mind Soothe Capsules as manufactured by Tong Jum Chew in Singapore, without establishing ingredient origins (HSA, 2025b). Product categories also have different requirements. Finished Chinese Proprietary Medicines (CPM) require listing and dealer licences; manufacturing and assembly facilities must meet Good Manufacturing Practice requirements (HSA, 2026b, 2026c). Raw or simply processed medicinal herbs are Chinese medicinal materials, while permitted ingredients in culinary soups or drinks for non-medicinal use are food products (Singapore Food Agency, 2025). Local manufacture therefore does not determine a product’s regulatory category.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00068",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[57]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 10244,
      "endIndex": 10284,
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_2",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "5.2 Packaging and the language of trust",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00069",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[58]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 10284,
      "endIndex": 10867,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Packaging makes product information visible to shoppers. CPM labels require English; Chinese may be added, while other languages must match approved English. Product names, ingredients, batch numbers, expiry dates and manufacturer, importer or assembler details help identify products and trace their supply chains (HSA, 2025a, section 5). These details can support trust, but HSA listing concerns safety and quality, rather than proving effectiveness or individual suitability (HSA, 2026b). Consumer guidance also highlights possible interactions with other medicines (HSA, 2026d).",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00070",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[59]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 10867,
      "endIndex": 11445,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Staff emphasised fresh colour and sulphur-free materials. Photographs show HSA signage, a sulphur-free Dang Shen claim and a separate American ginseng label. The Dang Shen label makes a processing claim; the ginseng label identifies the product. These messages may reassure shoppers, although photographs cannot verify the claims. HSA also warns against describing supplements as safe simply because they are natural (HSA, 2026a). Packaging therefore helps explain how trust is communicated, while the accuracy of claims and suitability for a buyer require separate assessment.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00071",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[60]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 11445,
      "endIndex": 11450,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "[INLINE_OBJECT kix.c359rnuto9ey]  [INLINE_OBJECT kix.8uejwrks5qo0]",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00072",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[61]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 11450,
      "endIndex": 11491,
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_2",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "5.3 Different shoppers in a shared space",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00073",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[62]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 11491,
      "endIndex": 11926,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "The staff member described most customers as Chinese, adding that some Malay customers bought dessert ingredients and some Indian customers bought nuts. These everyday foods may give different communities familiar reasons to enter a medicine hall without requiring shared knowledge of TCM. The mix of foods and medicinal products suggests that the shop can serve overlapping household purposes, rather than a single cultural practice.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00074",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[63]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 11926,
      "endIndex": 12393,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Course material on senna shows that the same plant can have different meanings in Chinese and Malay medicine (GEC1044 Lecture 5, n.d.). This provides a way to interpret the shared space: access to similar materials need not imply identical understandings of health or use. However, purchases alone cannot establish cultural exchange or shoppers’ beliefs. Customer interviews would be needed to understand whether people regard the products as food, medicine or both.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00075",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[64]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 12393,
      "endIndex": 12439,
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_1",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "6 Retail adaptation and individual assessment",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00076",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[65]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 12439,
      "endIndex": 12885,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Food gives herbs a household purpose, prepared packs reduce effort, and packaging communicates reported uses. Local branding and confirmed manufacture connect products with Singapore’s retail setting. Unschuld (2018) describes medicine adapting to social and political environments; Yang (2022) traces Singapore’s modernisation through state, professional and religious influences. Together, these accounts frame the shop’s everyday adaptations.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00077",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[66]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 12885,
      "endIndex": 13426,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Retail access remains distinct from treatment. PolyU’s reference profile lists ginseng as neutral (Table A1) and American ginseng as cool and Yin-nourishing; staff associations between fatigue and tonics (Table A6) cannot establish suitability. Pattern differentiation (辨证论治) requires fuller assessment of signs and symptoms (WHO, 2022). Nearly 40% of TCM users in the 2022 National Population Health Survey also used Western medicine for the same condition (Ministry of Health [MOH], 2025), situating household purchases within wider care.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00078",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[67]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 13426,
      "endIndex": 13440,
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_1",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "7 Limitations",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00079",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[68]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 13440,
      "endIndex": 13931,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "One visit and interview cannot establish demand trends or customer interpretations. Complete recipes, sourcing and purchasing records were unavailable. Mind Soothe has a confirmed Singapore manufacturing link, but ingredient origins remain unknown; staff named the category rather than the brand. Physician presence was unclear, and no consultation, prescription or outcome was recorded. Practitioner regulation provides background, without verifying an outlet physician’s role (MOH, 2026).",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00080",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[69]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 13931,
      "endIndex": 14104,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Reference profiles and external examples are distinguished from field observations. Sales records, custo